 "props": [
  {
   "id": "p_banecha_chatu",
   "gloss_en": "in the future the Holy One will say to Abraham (and then to Jacob, and to Isaac): your children have sinned against Me",
   "content": null,
   "locus": "Shabbat.89b.4",
   "daf": "89b",
   "sentenceId": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "p_yimachu",
   "gloss_en": "Master of the world, let them be wiped out for the sanctification of Your name",
   "content": null,
   "locus": "Shabbat.89b.4",
   "daf": "89b",
   "sentenceId": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "p_eimar_leyaakov",
   "gloss_en": "the Holy One: I will say it to Jacob, who had the pain of raising children; perhaps he will ask mercy for them",
   "content": null,
   "locus": "Shabbat.89b.4",
   "daf": "89b",
   "sentenceId": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "p_lo_besavei_taama",
   "gloss_en": "the Holy One: there is no sense in the old and no counsel in the young",
   "content": null,
   "locus": "Shabbat.89b.4",
   "daf": "89b",
   "sentenceId": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "p_banai_velo_banecha",
   "gloss_en": "Isaac: Master of the world, my children and not Your children? when they put 'we will do' before 'we will hear' You called them 'My son, My firstborn' (Ex 4:22); now -- my children and not Your children?",
   "content": null,
   "locus": "Shabbat.89b.4",
   "daf": "89b",
   "sentenceId": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "p_kama_chatu",
   "gloss_en": "Isaac: moreover, how much have they sinned? a man's years are seventy; take away twenty for which You do not punish -- fifty remain; take away twenty-five of nights -- twenty-five remain; take away twelve and a half of praying, eating and the privy -- twelve and a half remain",
   "content": null,
   "locus": "Shabbat.89b.5",
   "daf": "89b",
   "sentenceId": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "p_palga_alai",
   "gloss_en": "Isaac: if You bear them all, good; and if not, half on me and half on You; and if You say all of them on me -- here, I offered myself before You",
   "content": null,
   "locus": "Shabbat.89b.5",
   "daf": "89b",
   "sentenceId": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "p_ki_ata_avinu_leyitzchak",
   "gloss_en": "R' Yonatan: [this is] 'for You are our Father' -- Israel open and say it [to Isaac]",
   "content": {
    "pred": "verse_teaches",
    "args": [
     "ki_ata_avinu",
     "yisrael_omrim_leyitzchak"
    ]
   },
   "locus": "Shabbat.89b.5",
   "daf": "89b",
   "sentenceId": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "p_kalsu_lehkbh",
   "gloss_en": "Isaac: rather than praising me, praise the Holy One -- and Isaac shows them the Holy One with his eye",
   "content": null,
   "locus": "Shabbat.89b.5",
   "daf": "89b",
   "sentenceId": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "p_ata_hashem_avinu",
   "gloss_en": "R' Yonatan: [this is] 'You, Lord, are our Father, our Redeemer, from of old is Your name' -- at once Israel lift their eyes on high and say it",
